From f89b06e9312256739f9cc6204d099da4b28497f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RDoom <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:37:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 39/62] Switch: game thread never waits for the SD card; one
 decode per sprite, held frames

- Log files the game thread writes (rdoom.log, engine.log, engine-stderr.log,
  perf.log): their stdio flushes go to memory and the background writer
  writes them to the descriptor. Before, the writer's fflush held the stdio
  lock / log mutex during the SD write and any log line meanwhile (session
  report every 600 frames, list saves, pickups) stalled 90-150 ms.
- Sprites: the render thread checks whether a picture is ready without
  creating anything; if not, the actor keeps its previous picture (no
  flicker) and the game thread requests it next frame. The decode for the
  upload also gives the border trim (FTexture::TrimBuffer), so each picture
  is decoded once; synchronous uploads deliver the trim too.
- Uploads only at frame start, requests before prefetches, 3 ms budget;
  two nx_jobs workers; rd_sprite_prefetch switch.
- gl_precache on (walls/flats behind the loading screen); with background
  sprite decoding the precache skips every frame of every actor class.
  Saved configs get the new defaults once (rd_defaults_rev).
- Dynamic resolution rises after 45 frames without a missed vsync (the
  wait for frame N-2 includes the display queue under vsync and kept the
  scale at 60%); a scale that fails right after a rise is blocked 20 s.
- perf.log: BeginFrame and frame N-2 wait columns.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
